{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T01:43:06.212Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"7a4af4b641f1e7f9180f8b98","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-gh1715","claim:pm-jbplbq","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-998juj+pm-gh1715+pm-jbplbq","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-998juj","claim:pm-gh1715","claim:pm-jbplbq","lineage:pm-998juj","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rpucvb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A history stream with both a non-record line and a chain break has no pm recovery: salvage needs a verified chain and repair reads through the refusing decoder"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while fixing pm-jbplbq on 2026-11-21. The shared decoder now refuses a line that is valid JSON but not an object with history_record_invalid, and names pm history-repair <id> --salvage-tail as the recovery. Salvage removes a JSON null, boolean or number line wherever it sits, but it still requires the retained records to verify (inspectHistoryTail refuses with 'History salvage requires a nonempty verified prefix'). pm history-repair, with or without --append-only, reads through the decoder, so it refuses before it can repair the chain. A stream with both faults, for example an out-of-band edit followed by a tool that appended null, therefore has no pm-native recovery, and the only way out is restoring the stream from version control. Fix: let salvage remove scalar lines without requiring a verified chain when no invalid suffix is discarded (removal cannot conceal a record), report the chain verdict honestly instead of the hard-coded verify_ok true, and leave chain repair to the next history-repair. Duplicate check: searched salvage, chain break, scalar and history repair; pm-jbplbq owns the refusal and the single-fault salvage, pm-gh1715 the append-only chain repair."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["history","recovery","robustness","salvage"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-21T01:43:06.212Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T01:43:06.212Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A stream with a JSON null line and a chain break recovers with pm history-repair <id> --salvage-tail followed by pm history-repair <id> --append-only, executed in a spec; Salvage that only removes scalar lines never requires a verified chain and reports the real verify_ok and verify_errors; Salvage that discards an invalid suffix keeps its verified-prefix requirement"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":80},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every combination of a non-record line and a chain break has a pm-native recovery sequence"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Salvage refuses because the chain does not verify, and history-repair refuses because the decoder refuses the line"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1715","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-21T01:43:06.212Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-jbplbq","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-21T01:43:06.212Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"1bdf7de97bed6d2a07f19827ab369c14d72d54bd621b442c1a6dd514714b95fa","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b59d62f555daff4df4577ffefd887a8291d690866093c0da23b8b1addf5dc048"}
