{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T11:55:06.687Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"27675b3cf25f0c8ca46c5936","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-03q389+pm-3os5p6+pm-rpucvb","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-o2kc","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T11:55:06.687Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-21T11:55:06.687Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation on branch fix/history-remedies-converge, 2026-11-21. In src/sdk/history/salvage.ts, inspectHistoryTail now separates the line scan (scanSalvageLines) from the chain judgment (judgeRetainedChain). Discarding an invalid suffix still requires a nonempty hash-verified prefix. Removing only lines that cannot hold a record (JSON null, boolean or number) no longer requires the chain to verify, because removal conceals nothing. The retained records then replay leniently for the id check and the ownership fallback, and the history_salvage record keeps the newest epoch a record declares, or none for an implicit stream. The result reports the real verdict: chain_drift_before, verify_ok and verify_errors, which were hard-coded to false, true and [] before. A history_chain_unverified warning names pm history-repair <id> --append-only --dry-run. A record-less stream (only scalar lines) still refuses. A broken chain with nothing to discard refuses with a next step naming the append-only repair preview. pm health then reports the stream as a bridgeable history_drift_chain_mismatch (pm-3os5p6), and the advised append-only repair bridges the break with the salvaged stream as a byte prefix. Proven in tests/integration/lifecycle/history-remedies.integration.spec.ts (the null line plus the bridgeable break, then salvage, append-only repair, a clean history_drift check and history --verify --strict-exit), together with the suffix refusal, the nothing-to-discard next step and the implicit-epoch case."}]}],"before_hash":"4eb420661eeb59b852d7e06beca4cef7b508b9f022259fd51c63a713aa10c8b9","after_hash":"bec196a4f6b6fc60598274ac765594540624f65db1615f8d2888f59ca1d2e2f6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6f5fa59454741a3c6232dfe0d55e5e3d5caa4b6014d08bef9aa7fec7661f9002"}
