{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T12:39:42.804Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"27675b3cf25f0c8ca46c5936","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rnrefn","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rnrefn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-03q389+pm-3os5p6+pm-rnrefn+pm-rpucvb","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rnrefn","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rnrefn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-21T12:39:42.804Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 1 on PR #1763, 2026-11-21. Fixed: (a) salvage checks the item identity at every replayed state, so a misfiled stream that names another item refuses even when a later delete cleared the id. (b) The salvage record is planned before the lock, so a preview refuses wherever the write would; a digest algorithm this pm cannot compute refuses typed with history_salvage_refused and the upgrade step. (c) The follow-up warning names the append-only preview and the rewriting preview for a break a bridge cannot repair. (d) Lenient replay skips a root replacement that leaves no item object instead of throwing, in replay.ts lenientApplyReplayPatch, which the rewriting repair shares. (e) A stream of only scalar lines salvages to an empty stream without a salvage record, and for a live item the warning names pm history-repair <id>, which rebuilds it (pm-3os5p6)."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T12:39:42.804Z"}],"before_hash":"9c8c1949b20d21907d8141ef1f1d277beb14f3d0ec00ba1666684dd83a642461","after_hash":"d6540ff360458eda8d5fc153dd9135b4462a2b8a9a6036f137c3a9f12c1518d4","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"12021574fcd104da0acf9f5727cb9f563e9ec6be66b1c12356b7723686898e19"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-21T13:58:37.013Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"27675b3cf25f0c8ca46c5936","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rnrefn","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rnrefn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-03q389+pm-3os5p6+pm-rnrefn+pm-rpucvb","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-03q389","claim:pm-3os5p6","claim:pm-rnrefn","claim:pm-rpucvb","lineage:pm-rnrefn","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-21T13:58:37.012Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review rounds 2 to 4 on PR #1763, 2026-11-21. Fixed in the shared lenient replay (replay.ts lenientApplyReplayPatch), which salvage and the rewriting repair both use. A patch may pass through a non-object root and restore the item. A patch that ends without an item root is a deletion when its entry is a delete, and replays as the canonical empty document. Any other such patch is replayed again, skipping only the ops that would leave no root, so the ops that did apply are kept. Salvage judges a verified chain's identity on its strict replay states, plans its record only when something will be removed, and gives restore advice for a malformed digest label and upgrade advice only for a well-formed unknown one."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-21T13:58:37.013Z"}],"before_hash":"d6540ff360458eda8d5fc153dd9135b4462a2b8a9a6036f137c3a9f12c1518d4","after_hash":"201a37583c750170a7d0e371c1405dd70e47c55157d6fcb7d1eba436e41d1fd2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"f8cb45750cbcd1bf1bccc478e9560b1dbc4b2b8a61cb938cbeb6bcd1e65b88cc"}
